virtio-console: a socket port's connection is not closed after a read that used the guest's
last receive buffer.

pci_vtcon_sock_rx reads into the guest's buffers while there are any. When the last one is
used the loop ends, and the code below it is the "close" label: the host's connection was
closed although nothing was wrong (found by reading the code, 2026-11-12, before using a port
for hyperMAC's agent in Windows guests; not observed). Return there.

--- a/usr.sbin/bhyve/pci_virtio_console.c
+++ b/usr.sbin/bhyve/pci_virtio_console.c
@@ -453,6 +453,7 @@
 	} while (vq_has_descs(vq));
 
 	vq_endchains(vq, 1);
+	return;
 
 close:
 	mevent_delete_close(sock->vss_conn_evp);
